  "description": "Salty, sour, spicy, and fragrant with turmeric and ginger, this braised fish is typically served with leafy greens and rice.",
  "notes": "Notes: Any small, oily fish can be used to make pinarasakan. If using larger fish, bone-in steaks are much more preferable over fillets.If the gravy is runny after 45 minutes, remove the fish to a platter and heat the sauce over high heat until thickened, about 2 minutes.\n\nMake-ahead and storage: Pinarasakan can be refrigerated in an airtight container for up to 5 days.",
